<<PlayBackgroundMusic Exciting_1>>
<<SetBGSprite "HutInterior">>

<<SetCharacterExpression "Kamla" "Smiling">>
Kamla: Don't rub the collar, beta—it will start shining like tin. Hair behind the ear now, lie down.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Serious">>
Raju: Is it sticking up again?

<<SetCharacterExpression "Kamla" "Smiling">>
Kamla: Like a stubborn blade of grass—there, good boy.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Serious">>
Raju: Baba… what time will they pin the sheets?

<<SetCharacterExpression "ShivPrasad" "Smiling">>
ShivPrasad: When the peon finishes his tea and finds the drawing pin—we'll reach before him and watch the wall like it owes us money.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Kamla" "Smiling">>
Kamla: Drink two sips, not more—too much water makes numbers blur.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Serious">>
Raju: My hands are sweaty.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Ramu" "Smiling">>
Ramu: That's because they remember holding a bat and a pencil on the same week—proud hands sweat early.

<<SetCharacterExpression "ShivPrasad" "Smiling">>
ShivPrasad: Pride can wait—today we read marks, then we decide what pride is allowed to say.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Kamla" "Smiling">>
Kamla: He studied till the fan scolded him, slept without stories, and woke before the milkman—that's the work we could do.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Ramu" "Smiling">>
Ramu: If your heart starts running when we see the crowd, breathe like the drum—in, hold, out—and look at the rusty nail on the old notice board, that's our anchor.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Serious">>
Raju: In… hold… out.

<<SetCharacterExpression "ShivPrasad" "Smiling">>
ShivPrasad: Anchor won't change the tide, but it keeps the boat from lying.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Ramu" "Neutral">>
Ramu: True. Listen, captain—whatever the paper says, you walk the same, straight without running or drooping. If it's good we thank it and go home; if not, we learn where the holes are and fill them—no big face, no small face.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Serious">>
Raju: Will you stand near me?

<<SetCharacterExpression "Ramu" "Smiling">>
Ramu: Like a shadow with laces.

<<SetCharacterExpression "ShivPrasad" "Smiling">>
ShivPrasad: One rule before we step out—we don't ask others their number, don't announce ours, or compare on the road. The wall is for reading; the lane is for walking.

<<SetCharacterExpression "ShivPrasad" "Smiling">>
ShivPrasad: We carry each other—not just today, but everyday.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Kamla" "Smiling">>
Kamla: And we walk together—no racing ahead, Ramu.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Ramu" "Smiling">>
Ramu: I'll keep pace—if I run, you pull my shirt.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Smiling">>
Raju: Promise.

<<SetCharacterExpression "ShivPrasad" "Smiling">>
ShivPrasad: Lock the door, then we go—we'll be early and quiet, let the wall do the talking.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Kamla" "Smiling">>
Kamla: Shoes tied?

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Smiling">>
Raju: Double knot.

<<SetCharacterExpression "ShivPrasad" "Smiling">>
ShivPrasad: Good—come, all of you.

<<HideAllCharacters>>
<<EndEvent>>
